{\bkmkend AAAAAABQQY}
{
\pard\plain \s61\li360\sa60\sb30\qj\widctlpar\qj\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Imports the given file into the given scene structure. The function is expected to throw an ImportErrorException if there is an error. If it terminates normally, the data in {\b aiScene} is expected to be correct. Override this function to implement the actual importing. \par
 The output scene must meet the following requirements:\par
 {
\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
At least a root node must be there, even if its only purpose is to reference one mesh. \par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b aiMesh::mPrimitiveTypes} may be 0. The types of primitives in the mesh are determined automatically in this case. \par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
the vertex data is stored in a pseudo-indexed "verbose" format. In fact this means that every vertex that is referenced by a face is unique. Or the other way round: a vertex index may not occur twice in a single {\b aiMesh}. \par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b aiAnimation::mDuration} may be -1. {\b Assimp} determines the length of the animation automatically in this case as the length of the longest animation channel. \par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b aiMesh::mBitangents} may be nullptr if tangents and normals are given. In this case bitangents are computed as the cross product between normal and tangent. \par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
There needn't be a material. If none is there a default material is generated. However, it is recommended practice for loaders to generate a default material for yourself that matches the default material setting for the file format better than {\b Assimp}'s generic default material. Note that default materials {\i should}  be named AI_DEFAULT_MATERIAL_NAME if they're just color-shaded or AI_DEFAULT_TEXTURED_MATERIAL_NAME if they define a (dummy) texture.  \par}
If the AI_SCENE_FLAGS_INCOMPLETE-Flag is {\b not}  set:{
\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
at least one mesh must be there \par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
there may be no meshes with 0 vertices or faces \par}
This won't be checked (except by the validation step): {\b Assimp} will crash if one of the conditions is not met!\par
{{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
Parameters\par}
\pard\plain \s81\li360\widctlpar\ql\adjustright \fs20\cgrid \trowd \trgaph108\trleft426\tblind426\trbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \trbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \trbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \trbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \trbrdrh\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \trbrdrv\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 
\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \clbrdrr \brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \cltxlrtb \cellx2187
\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \clbrdrr \brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf15 \cltxlrtb \cellx8748
\pard \widctlpar\intbl\adjustright
